    "problem": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "paper",
        "layout": "list",
        "numbered": false,
        "row_density": "compact",
        "eyebrow": "The problem",
        "heading": "Two rides, one pair of shoes.",
        "lede": "<p>A wet commute is not one event. It is a wet ride in, eight hours of a shoe not drying under a desk, and a wet ride home in the same kit.</p>"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "p1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Spray travels upward",
            "body": "<p>Most of what soaks a rider comes off the front wheel and the road surface, aimed straight at the ankle and the shoe opening.</p>"
          }
        },
        "p2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Overshoes leak where they close",
            "body": "<p>They are cut to go over a shoe, which means an opening at the ankle \u2014 which is exactly where the spray is going.</p>"
          }
        },
        "p3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Nothing dries at the office",
            "body": "<p>A cycling shoe under a desk for eight hours is a cycling shoe that is still wet at half past five.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "p1",
        "p2",
        "p3"
      ]
    },
    "answers": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "ink",
        "layout": "list",
        "numbered": true,
        "eyebrow": "What answers it",
        "heading": "Waterproofing that stays on the foot.",
        "head_note": "<p>Sealing a shoe from the outside is a losing geometry. This seals the foot instead, and the foot is inside all of it.</p>",
        "link_label": "The three layers, in section",
        "link_url": "/#construction"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "a1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The barrier is inside the shoe",
            "body": "<p>Spray that gets through the shoe or past an overshoe stops at the sock. What the shoe does or does not do stops being the deciding factor.</p>"
          }
        },
        "a2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "It works with the shoes you ride in",
            "body": "<p>No cleat compatibility to check and nothing to stretch over a sole. It goes under whatever you already clip or lace into.</p>"
          }
        },
        "a3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "It comes inside with you",
            "body": "<p>You are not carrying a wet overshoe around the building. The sock comes off with the rest of your kit.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "a1",
        "a2",
        "a3"
      ]
    },
